Subject: [PATCH] BookSync: retain the 0.11 catalog at upstream's new location

The final 2.0 base split the catalog into window/rows/screens/download helpers.
The 0.11 overlay owns that implementation's packed rows, offline window, download
boot return and cache refresh lifecycle. Keep its rc3 integration surface at the
new bookorbit/ location, before applying the ordered behavior patches. Remove the
split helpers so only one catalog implementation is compiled. This preserves the
0.11 behavior, including the offline paging and refresh crash fixes, on every reader.

